{#- A VIEW page: a heading, a definition, the games it gathers, and one mixed
    timeline of everything written about them. Two things take this shape —
    /t/ (a curated tagview, membership authored in tagviews.yaml) and /r/ (a
    rating rung, membership DERIVED by grouping subjects on their `rating:`) —
    and they differ only in where the member list comes from, which is settled
    by the time this renders. Sharing the body is the reason /r/ cost a
    template and not a page type.

    Callers set `view` (slug, title, glyph, description, members, entries,
    optional indexUrl) and `emptyLabel`. The `.tag-*` classes are structural
    and read as "view page" here, tagview or rung alike — see the tag-page
    block in style.css.

    `view.pager` (2026-11-11): past page 1 the header is the title, linked
    back to page 1, and the page number; the definition, the members and
    their blurbs are page 1's. -#}
<article class="tag">
  {%- if view.pager.number > 1 %}
  <header class="tag-head">
    <h1>{% if view.glyph %}<span class="view-glyph" aria-hidden="true">{{ view.glyph }}</span> {% endif %}<a href="{{ view.pager.first }}">{{ view.title }}</a></h1>
    <p class="post-subdate">page {{ view.pager.number }}</p>
  </header>
  {%- else %}
  <header class="tag-head">
    <h1>{% if view.glyph %}<span class="view-glyph" aria-hidden="true">{{ view.glyph }}</span> {% endif %}{{ view.title }}</h1>
    {% if view.description %}<p class="tag-desc">{{ view.description }}</p>{% endif %}
    {#- A rung is one step of a ladder, and a ladder is only legible whole. -#}
    {% if view.indexUrl %}<p class="tag-index"><a href="{{ view.indexUrl }}">the whole scale →</a></p>{% endif %}
    {% if view.backUrl %}<p class="tag-index"><a href="{{ view.backUrl }}">{{ view.backLabel }}</a></p>{% endif %}
    {#- Membership IS the definition of the view, so it goes at the top rather
        than being inferred from the timeline below. -#}
    {% if view.members | length %}
    <p class="tag-members">
      {#- A rung that spans media marks each member's medium (2026-10-25);
          a one-medium page goes without. -#}
      {% for member in view.members %}{% if view.mixed %}<span class="mico m-{{ member.group }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ member.group | groupNoun }}"></span> {% endif %}<a href="/s/{{ member.slug }}/">{{ member.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  {#- The tag's note (2026-11-13): blurbs/tags/<slug>.md, its own prose and
      its own `### Elsewhere` links. A rung has none. -#}
  {% if view.introHtml %}
  <section class="note-intro">{{ view.introHtml | safe }}</section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- Members' standing blurbs, above the timeline: undated, so they can't
      slot into the stream — they sit where the view's definition does. Each
      row carries the member's art and links home, same grammar as a
      fragment's meta line. Blurbs are written to fit, so full text here.

      Both lists are rows in the daily's shape since 2026-11-03: a .frag with
      the subject's art in the left column and the text in a .frag-body that
      gives the image column up as padding — the markup linkSubjects wraps a
      daily's sections in, so the shell's CSS (art | text | images, the
      phone's cover in the rail) applies here unchanged. Hat, on the log:
      "it's hard to see what game is being written about", and its text ran
      narrower than the front page's. The cover is the label now, at every
      width, so the 24px chip that led each meta line went. `subjectSky` is
      skyTag, the daily's own art: the cover, or the generated tile. Any change
      to the daily's shell has to be checked here too. -#}
  {#- Prose only (2026-11-13): a member's `### Elsewhere` links stay on its
      own page — links are never inherited. -#}
  {% set blurbed = view.members | selectattr("blurbProseHtml") | list %}
  {% if blurbed | length %}
  <section class="blurbs">
    {% for member in blurbed %}
    <div class="frag"{% if member.coverBox %} style="--box:{{ member.coverBox }}"{% endif %}>
      {{ member.slug | subjectSky | safe }}
      <div class="frag-body">
        <p class="fragment-meta">
          <a class="fragment-subject" href="/s/{{ member.slug }}/">{{ member.title }}</a>
        </p>
        {{ member.blurbProseHtml | safe }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}
  {%- endif %}

  {% if view.entries | length %}
  <section class="timeline">
    {%- set entries = view.entries %}
    {% include "timeline.njk" %}
  </section>
  {%- set pager = view.pager %}
  {%- include "pager.njk" %}
  {% elif not (blurbed | length) %}
    {% if view.members | length %}
  <p class="empty">Nothing written about these yet.</p>
    {% else %}
  <p class="empty">{{ emptyLabel }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</article>
